WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.319
When President Trump announced his plans
to move the U.S. embassy from Tel Aviv

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:12.450
to Jerusalem, "It is time to officially
recognize Jerusalem as the capital of

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.539
Israel." he reversed decades of consensus
about the status of Jerusalem. The

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:22.619
announcement sparked massive protests
among Palestinians and throughout the

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.940
Muslim world. Here are five things to
know about Jerusalem and why it's so contentious.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.500
Israel has controlled West
Jerusalem since 1949. During the Six-Day

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:45.899
War Israel captured East Jerusalem and
annexed that half of the city, but the

00:00:45.899 --> 00:00:50.850
international community considers East
Jerusalem occupied territory. In 1980

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:55.530
after Israel passed a law declaring a
united Jerusalem their capital, the

00:00:55.530 --> 00:01:00.390
United Nations condemned the annexation.
Palestinians want to divide the city and

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:05.189
make East Jerusalem the capital of a
future Palestinian state, while Israelis

00:01:05.189 --> 00:01:08.180
want a unified Jerusalem to be their
capital.

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:18.560
During peace process negotiations for the Oslo Accords, the issue of Jerusalem was initially set

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:26.040
aside to avoid derailing the talks. In
2000, during a new round of negotiations,

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:30.720
talks were upended when the leaders of
Palestine and Israel disputed who would

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.160
control the maze of tunnels under
Jerusalem.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.940
Control of Jerusalem has been a trigger

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.720
for violence many times in the past. The
contested area of East Jerusalem is home

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.149
to some of the holiest sites in the
world

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:53.130
for Jews and Muslims. It is the site
where Judaism's two sacred temples once

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:57.659
stood and the site where the Prophet
Mohammed ascended to heaven. The trouble

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:02.399
is that the sites for Muslims and Jews
exist on the same land. There's a

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:07.259
precarious power share in place: Israeli
officials control who has access to the

00:02:07.259 --> 00:02:10.869
complex, but Muslims have religious
control inside.

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:15.269
Jews can enter but, aren't allowed to
pray. Instead, they use the Western Wall.

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:21.099
The Second Intifada began in 2000 when
then-opposition leader Ariel Sharon

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:24.700
visited the Temple Mount, to assert
Israel's right to the complex.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:31.360
Palestinians protested and were met with
tear gas and rubber bullets. The violence

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:37.569
lasted five years and killed over 3,000
Palestinians and nearly 1,000 Israelis,

00:02:37.569 --> 00:02:42.370
with thousands more wounded.
More recently, Israel set up metal

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:46.630
detectors to enter the complex, which
Palestinians say restricted access to

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:50.480
the holy site, sparking a new round of
protests and violence.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.200
In the early '70s sixteen countries had

00:02:58.209 --> 00:03:02.410
embassies including the Netherlands,
Costa Rica, Colombia, but after the UN

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:06.549
Security Council condemned the
annexation of East Jerusalem in 1980,

00:03:06.549 --> 00:03:12.610
member states left. Now Jerusalem only
has consulates - the U.S. would be the first

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.780
country to have an embassy back in the
city.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:22.600
Though Congress passed a law to

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:27.040
relocate the U.S. embassy to Jerusalem
more than 20 years ago, the law includes

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:31.180
a loophole that allows the president to
delay the relocation for the sake of

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.930
national security.
Every sitting president, Clinton, Bush,

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:40.419
Obama, has used this power and signed the
waiver every six months. President Trump

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:47.109
signed the waiver in June 2017 and again
in December 2017, but also signaled he

00:03:47.109 --> 00:03:51.150
would begin the process of moving the
embassy from Tel Aviv to Jerusalem.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:55.780
President Trump was careful not to call
Jerusalem the undivided capital of

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.530
Israel, but opposition to Trump's
declarations and the proposed embassy

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:03.970
move grows. Muslim countries worldwide
urge the recognition of East Jerusalem

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:08.799
as the capital of a future Palestinian
state. In Jerusalem, tensions are higher

00:04:08.799 --> 00:04:13.359
than usual. Palestinian militant group
Hamas has started launching rockets into

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:16.970
Israel from Gaza and calling for a third
Intifada.

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:21.860
Israel has arrested Palestinians and is
clamping down on protests and as lines

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:25.960
are drawn and the fight for Jerusalem
intensifies, the future of

00:04:25.960 --> 00:04:29.320
israeli-palestinian stability is once
again at risk.

